      "rule_id": "ruff:B006",
      "cwe_id": null,
      "title": "B006: Do not use mutable data structures for argument defaults",
      "explanation": "Do not use mutable data structures for argument defaults\nContextual assessment: The function definition `def collect(item, items=[])` uses a mutable list `[]` as its default argument value. Default argument expressions are evaluated once when the function definition is executed, meaning the same list instance is shared across every call that does not pass an explicit `items` argument.",
      "user_impact": "Subsequent calls to `collect(x)` without providing `items` will accumulate items across invocations instead of returning a fresh list containing only the current item, causing unintended data leakage and unexpected behavior.",
      "severity": "high",
